<h2> In volleyball, there are many rules which are split into two catergories, basic
rules and violations. <h2>
<h3> Some Basic Rules</h3>

<ul>
	<li>Only 6 players can be on the court (3 in the front row, 3 in the back)</li>
	<li>A player cannot hit touch the ball 2 times in a row (blocking does not count)</li>
	<li>You can make contact with the ball with any part of your body</li>
	<li>A ball may be played of the net</li>
	<li>The ball cannot hit the antennaa, the referee stand or the ceiling</li>
	<li>Matches are made out of 2 to 3 sets depending on the level of play. In a 3 set match 2 sets go to
	25 points and the last set goes to 15</li>
	</ul>
<h3> Some Violations </h3>

<ul>
	<li>Contacting the ball illegaly(double touches, carrying, throwing)</li>
	<li>Touching the net</li>
	<li>Crossing the court centerline</li>
	<li>Serving out of rotation</li>
	<li>Backrow player blocking</li>
</div>
